# Exploring the Infinite: A Guided Laboratory

Begin with the core surprise: an infinite collection may match a proper part of itself, yet it can never match its own family of subsets. [Cantor's theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor%27s_theorem) explains why.

## 1. Defeat any proposed list

A proposed list assigns one subset to each index. Change the membership decision at each matching index and the resulting diagonal subset differs from every listed row.

