<details><summary>Reveal the proof of diagonal escape</summary>
For a map $f:X\to\mathcal P(X)$, set $D=\{x:x\notin f(x)\}$. If $D=f(a)$, then $a\in D$ exactly when $a\notin D$, a contradiction. Thus no map from $X$ onto all its subsets exists.
</details>

