<details><summary>Background: injections, bijections, and strict size</summary>
An injection gives $|X|\leq|Y|$; a bijection gives equality. Singleton formation injects $X$ into $\mathcal P(X)$, while the diagonal proof forbids equality. Therefore $|X|<|\mathcal P(X)|$.
</details>

## 3. Compare two meanings of “next”

The successor cardinal $\kappa^+$ is the least cardinal above $\kappa$. The power-set cardinal $2^\kappa$ is always above $\kappa$, but may jump farther. At $\aleph_0$, asking whether the jump is immediate is the [continuum hypothesis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continuum_hypothesis).

